  "system": {
    "biography": "<p><strong>A gang punk turned samurai on Ludivenko's money.</strong> Diablo is the razorguy at the first meet (<em>Off and Running</em>, p.8&ndash;10), riding escort for the Johnson's Toyota Elite. He backs up the Company Man if trouble breaks out, and otherwise stays quiet. If the runners turn violent, he and the chauffeur lay down cover while Mr. Johnson gets clear.</p><p><strong>He is the runners' contact line.</strong> Diablo hands over his wristphone number so the team can reach their employers &mdash; which makes him the obvious thread to pull if they later want to work out who really hired them.</p><p><strong>On his sheet:</strong> the <strong>Uzi III</strong> the adventure gives him, fitted with shock pads and a Smartgun Adapter to pair with his Smartlink; an <strong>armored vest with plates</strong> (4/3); his <strong>retractable razors</strong> at 7L; and the gun on the <strong>Harley</strong> &mdash; which is the whole reason the adventure bothers to give him Gunnery 4. The Harley's weapon is listed as an Ingram Valiant because the book never says what it is; swap it freely. The <strong>Ares Predator</strong> and <strong>stun baton</strong> come with the Street Samurai archetype QE points at.</p>",
