        "notes": "Light machine gun, belt-fed 50 (c). Popular with merc units worldwide; the most common LMG model. Has a hip-brace recoil pad (Rating 1) and an ammunition bin slung over the shoulder. The only entry the book's Light Machine Guns section lists — there is no generic LMG. Light Machine Guns is a FIREARMS concentration (p.70); Gunnery governs heavy weapons \"on tripods, vehicle mounts, pintles, or in fixed emplacements\", so a VEHICLE-MOUNTED Valiant is fired with Gunnery even though the weapon itself is a firearm. SR2E p.238, p.255.<p><em>Queen Euphoria conversion (core p.283, method A — substitute the SR2 item). Printed SR1 code: <code>5S3</code>. The PRC-42D's nose gun (p.16). NOTE: methods disagree here — A gives 7S, B gives 8S. A wins on p.283's preference ordering. Re-check if the mislabelled Light_Machine_Gun_Generic file in the system pack resolves to a different weapon.</em></p>",
        "streetIndex": 2
      }
